    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d693">

                <pb facs="0560" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1698.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to my note of the 1st
                        instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d693-f1"/> I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that by direction of the Secretary of War the Adjutant General of the
                    Army sent on the 6th instant to the commanding general, Department of Colorado,
                    a telegram authorizing and directing him to release all Mexican Federal soldiers
                    who were being held by him, but to retain all arms, ammunition, and munitions of
                    war, and stating that said soldiers should be received by the commanding
                    officer, Agua Prieta, on the border.</p>
                <p>The arms, ammunition, and munitions of war will be held awaiting a further
                    investigation.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>.)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Chandler Hale.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
